%% HTTP prefix: /api/v1. API lane includes verified middleware and errorHandler.
%% Grouped read and validation calls short-circuit on error. No Repository layer is implied.
%% Support Coach uses POST /classes/:id/coaches/support. Session substitution is a separate use case.
%% assignCoach rechecks overlap but does not call validateResources or an approved-leave query here. Those additional checks are enforced when scheduling.
sequenceDiagram
    actor A as Center Manager
    participant UI as CoachAssignmentForm
    participant API as Express middleware / errorHandler
    participant C as classesController
    participant S as classesService
    participant DB as Prisma / PostgreSQL

    A->>UI: Choose primary Coach for class
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/classes/:id/coaches
    activate API
    API->>API: authenticate, checkFacilityScope, authorizeExact(MANAGER), validate request
    alt request guard rejects
        API-->>UI: 400 / 401 / 403 error
    else request accepted
        API->>C: assignCoach(req, res, next)
        activate C
        C->>S: assignCoach(classId, coachId, isPrimary)
        activate S
        S->>DB: Read class, active Coach, facility staff assignment, specializations and upcoming schedule conflicts
        activate DB
        DB-->>S: Requested records and validation context
        deactivate DB
        S->>S: Require matching facility and sport expertise, reject upcoming schedule overlap
        S->>S: Lock class assignment and target Coach, recheck overlap before changing primary assignment
        alt class / Coach missing, expertise mismatch or resource conflict
            S-->>C: 400 / 404 / 409
        else business conditions satisfied
            S->>DB: Transaction unsets previous primary and upserts ClassMember with requested isPrimary
            activate DB
            DB-->>S: Saved result
            deactivate DB
            S->>S: notifyCoachChange after assignment persistence
            S-->>C: Updated class Coach assignment
        end
        deactivate S
        C-->>API: response or next(error)
        deactivate C
        API-->>UI: 200 result or mapped error
    end
    deactivate API
    UI-->>A: Show result or actionable error

